verage":20.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":3.1806798242950207,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":18.2,"_gate_accruals":-0.01628570135679782,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":21.1,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.13525050781217854,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":75.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.008731239800715718,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":89.1,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.06069932723386759,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":30.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4854718641312197,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":19.1,"_gate_incr_roic":0.11981522389718824,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":56.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.3709066268921072,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0109922567337003,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":35.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10274852364071285,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":76.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.014018531655311972,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":18.0,"_gate_margins":-0.010270662365140936,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":39.7,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.023926152331423003,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03971026328718985,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":99.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.022665164739092348,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":62.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.03782,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":25.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Corpay, Inc. operates as a payments company that helps businesses and consumers to manage and pay their expenses.\nIt operates through Corporate Payments, Vehicle Payments, Lodging Payments, and Other segments. The company offers vehicle payment solutions for fuel, tolls and parking, vehicle compliance, auto insurance and road assistance, fleet maintenance, and long-haul transportation services, as well as prepaid food and transportation vouchers and cards. It also provides corporate payment solutions, such as cross-border payments, spend management solutions, AP modernization, virtual cards, and purchasing and T&E cards. Additionally, it offers lodging payments solutions for employees who travel overnight for work purposes; traveling crews and stranded passengers from airlines and cruise lines; workforce lodging solutions for business travel programs; airline logistics, crew management, insurance, and other payments solutions. Further, the company offers gifts and payroll cards. It serves business, merchant, consumer, and payment network customers. The company was formerly known as FLEETCOR Technologies, Inc. and changed its name to Corpay, Inc. in June 2002. Corpay, Inc. was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ronald F. Clarke | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 69 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $384K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $110K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Corpay, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $29.9B market cap on $4.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.22007264813659239},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $146.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 37% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(CPAY) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/CPAY_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110526064602_1793922362.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793922362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Corpay (CPAY) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/corpay-cpay-q3-2026-earnings-180236000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902341.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why is Corpay (CPAY) stock rocketing higher today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/cpay/news/why-up-down/why-is-corpay-cpay-stock-rocketing-higher-today","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793900436.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Corpay (CPAY) Stock May Be 40% Undervalued After Q3 Earnings Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-cpay/corpay/news/corpay-cpay-stock-may-be-40-undervalued-after-q3-earnings-be","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793881683.828,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.848,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Corpay to Participate in Upcoming Investor Conferences","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/corpay-participate-upcomi